    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d834">

                <pb facs="0776" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7490F/11–144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gallman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-01T20:00:00+01:00">November 1, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 2—12:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9453. The Embassy took up with the Foreign Office the contents of the
                    Department’s 8924 October 26, 2 p.m. Foreign Office tells us that the
                    Departmental Committee on Censorship in London on which Lt. Commander Patterson,
                    United States Navy, is a representative objected to the establishment of a Saudi
                    Arabian Government radio station on security grounds because the control of the
                    station would be in the hands of the Saudi Arabian Government. The Foreign
                    Office also stated that Mr. Berle<anchor n="99" xml:id="d834-f1"/> had discussed
                    this matter with the British Embassy in Washington and that the Foreign Office
                    would prefer that this whole question be handled through that channel.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gallman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d834-f1" n="99" xml:id="d834-f1-content">
                <p>Adolf A. Berle, Jr., Assistant Secretary of State.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
